  "brief": "<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Market Overview</h2>\n\nFutures are painting red across the board with small-caps taking the biggest hit down 1.03% as Iran tensions keep markets on edge. VIX climbing to 27.38 signals continued uncertainty, while the divergence between tech (+0.34%) and cyclicals tells the defensive rotation story clearly.\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> What to Watch</h2>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>ADP Employment Change (12:15 ET)</strong> - Weekly jobs data could shift Fed expectations with Waller speaking later today</li>\n<li><strong>Fed Waller Speech (1:00 PM ET)</strong> - Hawkish commentary could accelerate the tech rotation we're seeing pre-market</li>\n<li><strong>Pending Home Sales (2:00 PM ET)</strong> - Housing weakness would amplify recession fears already brewing from geopolitical stress</li>\n<li><strong>Iran Peace Proposal</strong> - Reparations demand and troop withdrawal conditions suggest this rally on \"peace talks\" is premature</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-amber\"><div class=\"callout-label\">⚡ Key Driver</div>G7 finance ministers meeting on Iran fallout response - any coordinated action announcement could swing markets violently either direction</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Sector Rotation</h2>\n\nClassic flight-to-quality setup with tech leading while cyclicals get hammered. Materials down 2.07% and consumer discretionary off 1.49% as investors price in economic damage from prolonged Middle East conflict. Energy flat despite tensions suggests supply disruption fears are overblown or already priced.\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-red\"><div class=\"callout-label\">⚠ Bear Case</div>Small-cap weakness (IWM -1.03%) signals broad economic pessimism beyond just geopolitical noise - domestic growth concerns building</div>\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-green\"><div class=\"callout-label\">✦ Bull Case</div>Tech strength shows quality names can outperform even in risk-off environments - defensive growth trade intact</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Levels That Matter</h2>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>SPY 730</strong> - Critical support from April lows, break signals deeper correction incoming</li>\n<li><strong>QQQ 710</strong> - Tech holding above this level keeps defensive rotation thesis alive</li>\n<li><strong>VIX 30</strong> - Breach above triggers systematic de-risking across momentum strategies</li>\n<li><strong>IWM 270</strong> - Small-cap breakdown level would confirm broad risk-off acceleration</li>\n</ul>\n\n<hr>\n<p><em>Not a prediction. A preparation. Make your plan before the bell.</em></p>"
